Chapter: DeskChromeIconsTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopFont
  cites Works chapter GopPrograms
  cites Works chapter GopIcon
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The chrome and launcher icons are painted after the layout, keyed on
 `wn-id`. That is what keeps them out of the hit test, and it is also what
 makes them fail SILENTLY: `desk-icon-on` answers 0 for an id the tree does
 not carry, so renaming a button removes its icon and nothing says so. This
 asserts every id the paint asks for is one the tree answers.

 The absent row is the control. Without it a walk that found nothing would
 report the same shape as one that found everything, since both would print
 a number equal to their own denominator.

 THE PAINTER IS HANDED TWO DIFFERENT TREES AND THE COUNT HAS TO SAY WHICH.
 `desk-chrome-icons` runs from `dk-chrome-paint`, which paints the desktop
 chrome and also the start menu, so its two ids live in different trees:
 `menu` is in the taskbar and `shutdown` is in the menu's body. Counted
 against the desktop alone that reads `1 of 2`, which is the same shape a
 genuinely missing icon gives -- the exact confusion this file exists to stop.
 So each id is counted against the tree it belongs to, and the two cross rows
 are printed because they say opposite things and both are load-bearing.
 `shutdown` MUST be absent from the desktop: a desktop carrying a Shutdown
 button is what the sidebar was. `menu` MUST still be present while the start
 menu is up, because `desk-chrome-face` wraps both trees and the taskbar is
 under the menu either way -- which is what keeps the pill there to dismiss
 it. The second row was written expecting a 0 and the run said 1; the run was
 right.

  dci-found : WidgetNode, Text -> Integer
  dci-found (root) (id) =
    when widget-find root id
      is Just (n) -> 1
      is None -> 0

  dci-chrome-ids : List Text = ["menu", "shutdown"]

  dci-count : WidgetNode, List Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dci-count (root) (ids) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length ids then acc
    else dci-count root ids (i + 1) (acc + dci-found root (list-at ids i))

  dci-rows : WidgetNode, List GprEntry, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dci-rows (root) (es) (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let e = list-at es i
    in dci-rows root es n (i + 1) (acc + dci-found root ("gpr-" & e.ge-label))

  dci-ds : Integer
  dci-ds = alloc-zeroed 256 64

  dci-ps : Integer
  dci-ps = alloc-zeroed 64 64

  dci-chrome : Text
  dci-chrome =
    let ds = dci-ds
    in let root = desk-chrome-with (widget-panel "content" DirColumn 0 []) 1024 ds
    in let menu = desk-chrome-with (desk-menu-tree dci-ps gfont-none 1) 1024 ds
    in let ids = dci-chrome-ids
    in let both = dci-found root "menu" + dci-found menu "shutdown"
    in let absent = dci-found root "no-such-button"
    in "chrome=" & show both & " of " & show (list-length ids) & "   absent=" & show absent
       & "   shutdown off the desktop=" & show (dci-found root "shutdown")
       & "   pill still under the start menu=" & show (dci-found menu "menu")

 The window shows every entry and the start menu shows the OPEN group's, so
 the two denominators differ on purpose. A menu row count equal to the whole
 register would mean the collapse had stopped collapsing, and one of zero
 would mean `desk-gpr-icons` had lost the tree it paints into; the window row
 beside it is what separates those from a change to the ids themselves.

  dci-launcher : Text
  dci-launcher =
    let ps = dci-ps
    in let root = gpr-tree ps
    in let es = gpr-entries
    in let n = list-length es
    in let hit = dci-rows root es n 0 0
    in let mhit = dci-rows (gpr-menu-tree ps) es n 0 0
    in "window rows=" & show hit & " of " & show n & "   menu rows=" & show mhit & " of " & show n & " (the open group)"

 The gutter must be WIDER than the icon or the label sits flush against it,
 which is what the first version on the glass did. One cell of daylight is
 the whole assertion.

  dci-gutter : Text
  dci-gutter =
    "mark=" & show gpr-mark-cells & " icon=" & show gpr-icon-cells & " gutter=" & show (text-length gpr-gutter) & " gap=" & show (text-length gpr-gutter - gpr-icon-cells)

 EVERY PANE THAT CAN BE MINIMISED MUST HAVE A PILL ICON, AND IT MUST NOT BE
 THE FALLBACK. `dk-pill-icon` is keyed by focus id in the same arm order as
 `desk-wnd-title`, so the failure to catch is an id present in one and absent
 from the other. That reads as an empty name, `gicon-named` answers the `file`
 icon for it, and the pill draws a plausible picture. A misspelled name lands
 on exactly the same fallback, so ONE row covers both: for every id the title
 table names, the icon must be non-empty and must resolve to ITSELF.

 `file` is not used deliberately by any pane, which is what makes it usable as
 the sentinel here. Files takes `folder` and Edit takes `edit`. If a pane ever
 genuinely wants `file`, this row stops discriminating and has to change.

  dci-pill-ids : List Integer = [desk-focus-clkp, desk-focus-calc, desk-focus-con, desk-focus-prog, desk-focus-cal, desk-focus-dif, desk-focus-style, desk-focus-trk, desk-focus-mon, desk-focus-scene, desk-focus-fish, desk-focus-bro, desk-focus-files, desk-focus-edit]

  dci-pill-ok : Integer -> Integer
  dci-pill-ok (fid) =
    let n = dk-pill-icon fid
    in if text-length n == 0 then 0
    else if (gicon-named n).ico-name /= n then 0
    else 1

  dci-pill-count : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dci-pill-count (ids) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else dci-pill-count ids (i + 1) n (acc + dci-pill-ok (list-at ids i))

  dci-pills : Text
  dci-pills =
    let ids = dci-pill-ids
    in let n = list-length ids
    in let ok = dci-pill-count ids 0 n 0
    in let titled = dci-titled ids 0 n 0
    in "pill icons=" & show ok & " of " & show n
       & "   titled=" & show titled
       & "   an untitled id falls back=" & (gicon-named (dk-pill-icon 0)).ico-name

  dci-titled : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dci-titled (ids) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else dci-titled ids (i + 1) n (acc + (if text-length (desk-wnd-title (list-at ids i)) == 0 then 0 else 1))

 An unknown name answers the file icon rather than refusing, so a row whose
 icon is misspelled still draws something. That is deliberate and it is
 asserted here so it cannot be quietly changed into a blank.

  dci-fallback : Text
  dci-fallback =
    let known = gicon-named "folder"
    in let unknown = gicon-named "no-such-icon"
    in "known=" & known.ico-name & " unknown=" & unknown.ico-name

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni dci-chrome
    print-line-uni dci-launcher
    print-line-uni dci-pills
    print-line-uni dci-gutter
    print-line-uni dci-fallback
  end
